// Problem — close paraphrase of Mel's answer to question 1.
---

<section id="problem">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">01 · The problem</p>
      <h2>Bookmarks aren't a knowledge base.</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <p>
        As a technical community leader, you collect links constantly — in chat, on
        calls, in slides, in your DMs. A month later, none of it is findable, none of
        it has context, and you have no way of knowing which links actually helped
        your people implement something versus which ones looked promising and weren't.
      </p>
      <p>
        The signal is real, but it's scattered. There is no durable record of
        <em>which</em> resource is good <em>for what</em>, who vouched for it, and
        how often it's been opened. So the same research gets re&#8209;done, week after week.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="note">
      You don't need another read&#8209;later app. You need an inbox that turns a URL into a
      tagged, reviewed, queryable entry — and that your agents can read like a database.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

